# Live Sight — personalized vision LoRA adapters

LoRA adapters for [Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct), trained nightly on a single user's interaction history. Built for [Live Sight](https://github.com/coderwhisperer/live-sight), a vision assistant for blind and low-vision users developed during the AMD Developer Hackathon (May 2026).

Each adapter represents a snapshot of the model adapting to one user's daily corrections, taken over five days of real usage in Karachi, Pakistan.

## Adapter versions

| Version | Trained on | Corrections | Final mean loss | Status |
|---------|------------|-------------|-----------------|--------|
| v0 | 9 examples | 0 | 0.061 | archived (pipeline validation) |
| v1 | 25 examples | 5 | 0.279 | fallback |
| v1.1 | 88 examples | 18 | 0.799 | fallback (failed — see below) |
| v1.2 | 21 examples (corrections only) | 21 | 0.660 | **active** |

All adapters: rank 16, alpha 32, target modules `q/k/v/o_proj` in language layers, `max_steps=100`, label-masked CE on assistant tokens.

Adapter file: ~29 MB (bf16 safetensors). Loaded via vLLM's runtime adapter API for hot-swapping.

## The v1.1 → v1.2 lesson

v1.1 was trained on the full 88-entry interaction corpus including 18 corrections. It performed worse than v1 because corrections were diluted by 50 short ask-mode entries ("yes", "black", "a keyboard") that gave each correction only ~4.5 epochs of gradient updates.

v1.2 used the same hyperparameters but filtered to the 21 corrections only — giving each correction ~16.8 epochs. It recovered v1's hero memorization pattern AND learned new corrections without the reading-order fragmentation v1.1 produced.

Lesson: at fixed compute, focused signal beats more data when the goal is per-example memorization for personalization.

## How to use

Load the active adapter via vLLM:

```python
# Server: serve Qwen3-VL-8B with --enable-lora
# Then load adapter at runtime:
import requests
requests.post('http://localhost:8000/v1/load_lora_adapter', json={
    'lora_name': 'livesight-v1_2',
    'lora_path': './adapters/v1_2',
})
```

Then route inference requests to model `livesight-v1_2`.

## Training data

Available on request via private dataset repo: [`friendly-coder-ai/live-sight-data`](https://huggingface.co/datasets/friendly-coder-ai/live-sight-data). Contains real interaction logs from Karachi, Pakistan including images of personal spaces and handwritten notes — kept private to respect user privacy.

## Limitations

- Trained on one user's data. Generalization to other users is the next research question, not the demo's claim.
- Image content reflects the user's environment (Karachi household, English/Roman Urdu mix). Adapter will likely perform worse on visual contexts not represented in training.
- v1.2 was tuned for demo memorization. For broader use, retraining with longer schedules on a more diverse corpus would be needed.

